Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-07
Subject: Use compiler-local PByte in aoptbase
License: expat

`compiler/aoptbase.pas` declares `TInstrSinceLastMod` in its interface using
`pbyte`, but it does not import the compiler unit that defines the compiler's
own `pbyte = ^byte` alias. Native FPC can resolve this through implicit
System.PByte, hiding the missing compiler-local dependency.

Import `globtype` explicitly so the translated bootstrap resolves the same
type through the compiler source instead of relying on a System alias.

--- a/compiler/aoptbase.pas
+++ b/compiler/aoptbase.pas
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
   interface
 
     uses
+      globtype,
       aasmbase,aasmcpu,aasmtai,aasmdata,
       cpubase,
       cgbase,
